      "text": "{\"twins\":[\"When `signer_kwargs=None` is passed, `Serializer.__init__` sets it to `dict(salt=self.salt)`.\",\"`Serializer.__init__` coerces `salt=None` to the default `b'itsdangerous.Serializer'` before storing it.\",\"In `Serializer.dumps` the payload is wrapped as `self.dump_payload(want_bytes(obj))`.\",\"`_CompactJSON.loads('{\\\"id\\\":5,\\\"name\\\":\\\"itsdangerous\\\"}')` returns `{'id': '5', 'name': 'itsdangerous'}`.\",\"When `signer=None` is passed, `Serializer.__init__` uses the class default signer, which for the plain serializer is `TimestampSigner`.\",\"`Signer.unsign` raises `BadSignature` with the message \\\"Separator b'.' missing from value\\\" when the separator is absent.\",\"`want_bytes` in encoding.py encodes text as UTF-8 with `errors='ignore'`.\",\"`Signer.verify_signature` loops over `self.secret_keys` in order, derives a key for each, and returns `True` on the first algorithm match, otherwise `False`.\",\"`HMACAlgorithm.get_signature` calls `hmac.new(key, msg=value, digestmod=self.digest_method)` and returns `mac.hexdigest()`.\",\"`URLSafeSerializerMixin.load_payload` delegates to `self.serializer.loads(json)`, bypassing the base `Serializer.load_payload`.\"]}",
